# LocalBoost AI — AI Agent Rules (Update-Safe Customization)

You are modifying a **modular Laravel 13 + Livewire 4** application (LocalBoost AI / marketing-local-hub). The author's business logic lives primarily in `modules/`, not a fat `app/`. Treat shipped code as **immutable core**. Always extend; never patch.

> **Stack snapshot** (do not change without explicit user approval):
> PHP `^8.3` · Laravel `^13.0` · Livewire `^4.1` · Fortify `^1.34` · Laravel AI `^0.4.2` · Stripe PHP `15.0` · AWS SDK `3.322.9` · Tailwind CSS v4 · Vite (per-theme) · Pest `^4.4` · Pint.

---

## 1. Strict core protection — NEVER edit these paths

| Zone | Path | Why it is core |
|------|------|----------------|
| Vendor | `vendor/**` | Composer-managed |
| Core modules | `modules/Admin*/**`, `modules/App*/**`, `modules/Payment*/**` | Author feature code (~70 modules) |
| Core app shell | `app/**` (entire `app/`, including `Providers/`, `Http/`, `Livewire/`, `Support/`, `Installer/`, `Concerns/`, `Console/`, `Exceptions/`, `Notifications/`) | Framework wiring & global registries |
| Core routes | `routes/web.php`, `routes/console.php`, `routes/settings.php`, `routes/public-storage.php`, `app/Installer/routes/**` | Author route map |
| Bootstrap | `bootstrap/app.php`, `bootstrap/providers.php` | Middleware pipeline + module auto-discovery |
| Core config | `config/*.php` | Override only via `.env` keys core already reads |
| Core themes | `resources/themes/app/default/**`, `resources/themes/guest/localboostai/**`, `resources/themes/shared/**` | Default UI; clone instead |
| Core DB | `database/migrations/2026_*_create_database.php`, `database/seeders/**` | Schema & demo data owned by author |
| Core lang | `lang/*.json` at project root | Extend with custom JSON loaded via `loadJsonTranslationsFrom` |
| Core public build | `public/build/themes/app/default/**`, `public/build/themes/guest/localboostai/**` | Author Vite manifests |
| Core tests | `tests/**` | Unless explicitly writing custom tests |
| Build / deploy | `Dockerfile`, `entrypoint.sh`, `composer.json`, `composer.lock`, `package.json`, `package-lock.json`, `artisan`, `index.php`, `public/index.php`, `.htaccess`, `.editorconfig`, `.gitattributes`, `.gitignore` | Touch only with explicit user approval |

**Hard rule:** if a change requires editing anything above, **stop** and re-route through an extension point in §3.

---

## 2. Allowed customization zones — ONLY edit here

| Purpose | Location |
|---------|----------|
| Custom feature module (preferred for page-sized work) | `modules/Custom{Feature}/` (mirror author module layout) |
| Custom global PHP | `app/Custom/` — `Http/`, `Livewire/`, `Support/`, `Services/`, `Providers/`, `Models/`, `Actions/`, `Observers/`, `database/migrations/`, `resources/views/`, `lang/` |
| Custom routes | `routes/custom.php` (loaded from your `App\Custom\Providers\CustomServiceProvider::boot()`) |
| Custom provider registration | **`bootstrap/providers.marketplace.php`** — already `require`d by `bootstrap/providers.php`; return extra provider class names here |
| Custom config | `config/custom.php` (load via `mergeConfigFrom` from your provider) |
| Custom views | `app/Custom/resources/views/`, `modules/Custom*/Resources/views/`, custom theme `resources/views/` |
| Custom theme | `resources/themes/app/custom/` and/or `resources/themes/guest/custom/` (with `theme.json`) — e.g. `resources/themes/guest/mlhubtheme/**` |
| Custom theme public assets (additive only) | `public/resources/themes/{area}/{your-theme}/` — copy **only** files the core serves via `theme_asset()` / `theme_asset_for()` (e.g. `preview.svg`); never replace or symlink the whole `public/resources/themes/` tree |
| Custom assets | Inside your custom theme: `assets/css/`, `assets/js/` → built by Vite to `public/build/themes/{area}/custom/` |
| Custom migrations | `app/Custom/database/migrations/` or `modules/Custom*/Database/Migrations/` |
| Custom translations | `app/Custom/lang/{locale}.json` (loaded via `loadJsonTranslationsFrom` in your provider) |

> **Critical wiring fact:** `bootstrap/providers.php` already calls `require __DIR__.'/providers.marketplace.php'` and merges its returned array into the provider list. **Never edit `bootstrap/providers.php`** — append your provider class names to `bootstrap/providers.marketplace.php` instead. (The file ships empty `return [];` — safe to append to.)

---

## 3. Extension strategy (in strict order of preference)

1. **Registry / helper hook** (zero new classes when possible):
   - Navigation: `register_sidebar_section`, `register_sidebar_item`, `register_user_sidebar_section`, `register_user_sidebar_item`
   - Header: `register_header_item`, `add_to_header`
   - Dashboard widgets: `register_admin_dashboard_item`, `register_user_dashboard_item`
   - Plans & limits: `register_plan_permission`, `\Pricing::add([...])`, `\Pricing::addSubFeatures([...])` inside `$this->app->booted()`
   - Credits / AI billing: `register_credit_action`, `consume_credits`, `credit_service()`
   - Settings page: `register_setting_item`
   - Cron: `afterResolving(SystemCronRegistry::class, fn ($r) => $r->register([...]))`
   - Payments: `PaymentGatewayDefinition` + `PaymentGatewaySettingsRegistry::register('key', [...])`
   - Admin menu labels/order: `OptionStore` (`admin_menu_sidebar_overrides`) via the admin **Menu Builder** UI (not Blade)
2. **New `modules/Custom{Feature}/` module** (auto-discovered by `bootstrap/providers.php` glob). Mirror layout of `modules/AppBusinessProfiles/`. Set `priority > 20` in `module.json` so your provider boots *after* core and last-write-wins for registries.
3. **Container rebind + child class** in your `CustomServiceProvider::register()`:
   ```php
   $this->app->bind(\Modules\X\Service::class, \App\Custom\Services\MyService::class);
   ```
4. **Livewire replacement** — custom Livewire class + *new* route in `routes/custom.php` with `Route::livewire(...)`. Do not edit module `Routes/web.php`.
5. **View augmentation** via `View::composer('vendor::view', fn ($v) => $v->with(...))`. For visual replacement, clone the Blade into a custom module's `Resources/views/` and render via custom Livewire.
6. **Fortify / auth** — subclass `Modules\AdminUser\Actions\Fortify\*` under `App\Custom\Actions\Fortify\…` and rebind via `Fortify::createUsersUsing(…)` etc. in your provider's `register()`.
7. **Eloquent observers** — register in `CustomServiceProvider::boot()`; modules expose few domain events.

> **Do NOT** introduce a Repository layer. The codebase uses `Support/` (stateless helpers, catalogs, registries) and `Services/` (transactional workflows). Match this.

---

## 4. Coding standards (match the codebase exactly)

- **PHP**: `^8.3`. Typed properties, return types, constructor property promotion. Use `declare(strict_types=1);` only when surrounding code uses it (most modules do not).
- **Style**: Laravel **Pint**. Run `vendor/bin/pint app/Custom modules/Custom*` — never reformat core.
- **Namespaces**: `App\Custom\…` → `app/Custom/`; `Modules\Custom{Feature}\…` → `modules/Custom{Feature}/` (PSR-4 already in `composer.json`).
- **Controllers**: thin; delegate to `Support/`, `Services/`, or Livewire.
- **Routes**:
  - Named, dot notation: `portal.{feature}`, `admin-{feature}.*`.
  - Portal middleware: `['web', 'auth', 'verified']`.
  - Pages prefer `Route::livewire('/path', SomeIndex::class)->name('portal....')`.
  - Read prefix from module config: `config('modules.{alias}.route_prefix', 'portal/...')`.
- **Config**: per-module `config/config.php` merged with `mergeConfigFrom(..., 'modules.{alias}')`.
- **Translations**: `__()` / `@lang` for every user-visible string.
- **Dates**: `CarbonImmutable` (set as default by `App\Providers\AppServiceProvider`).
- **Auth user**: `Modules\AdminUser\Models\User`.
- **Plans**: gate features with `auth()->user()?->canUsePlanFeature('localboost')` and `PlanLimitGuard`.
- **Demo mode**: any mutating Livewire action must remain compatible with `App\Livewire\DemoModeActionGuard` and `App\Http\Middleware\PreventDemoModeWriteOperations`.
- **Icons**: Font Awesome `fa-light`. Match existing classnames.
- **Components**: prefer `<x-ui.*>` (themed) and `<x-shared.*>` (cross-theme); never re-implement what exists.
- **Theme tokens**: use CSS variables (`var(--theme-accent-rgb)`, `var(--theme-header-text-color)`, `var(--theme-border-color-rgb)`, …) instead of hard-coded colors.

---

## 5. Module conventions (when creating `modules/Custom*`)

```
modules/CustomFoo/
  module.json                   # { "name": "CustomFoo", "providers": [...], "priority": 100 }
  Providers/CustomFooServiceProvider.php
  Routes/web.php
  Http/Controllers/             # only if not Livewire-only
  Livewire/
  Models/
  Support/                      # optional — helpers.php auto-loaded if present
  Services/                     # optional
  Resources/views/
  config/config.php             # route_prefix, feature flags
  Database/Migrations/
```

Provider order:
1. `register()`: `mergeConfigFrom(__DIR__.'/../config/config.php', 'modules.customfoo')` + container bindings.
2. `boot()`: `loadRoutesFrom`, `loadViewsFrom(..., 'customfoo')`, `loadMigrationsFrom`, optional `loadJsonTranslationsFrom`, registry calls (`register_*`), and `$this->app->booted(fn () => \Pricing::add([...]))` if plan-gated.

> `bootstrap/providers.php` auto-discovers each `modules/*` and `require_once`s `Support/helpers.php` if present.

---

## 6. Frontend rules

- Stack: **Blade + Livewire 4 + Alpine.js** (inline `x-data`). **No** React/Vue SPA.
- CSS: **Tailwind v4** via `@import` in theme `assets/css/app.css`. Use `var(--theme-*)` tokens.
- Assets: `theme_vite('app', ['assets/js/app.js', 'resources/themes/shared/js/highcharts.js'])` in layouts.
- **Never** edit `resources/themes/app/default/**`, `resources/themes/guest/localboostai/**`, or `resources/themes/shared/**`. Clone to `resources/themes/{area}/custom/`.
- Minor branding → Admin → Themes → **Custom CSS / Custom JS** fields (no rebuild needed).
- Custom Vite output must land in `public/build/themes/{area}/custom/`. Do not collide with core manifests.

---

## 7. Before every change

1. Identify the **smallest extension point** (registry > new module > rebind > route override > theme clone).
2. `git diff --name-only` must show zero entries outside the allowed zones in §2.
3. List new routes, permissions, migrations, env keys.
4. Document any container rebinds — these are the only fragile points across author updates.

---

## 8. Update-safe fixes (bugs, 404s, previews, deploy)

When fixing a bug or missing asset, **default to the narrowest change in a custom zone**. Author updates re-copy or overwrite core files; global patches and new root scripts break on the next merge.

### Prefer (smallest blast radius)

1. **Custom theme / module only** — edit `resources/themes/guest/{your-theme}/**`, `modules/Custom*/**`, or `app/Custom/**`.
2. **Additive public files for your theme only** — if core builds URLs like `asset('resources/themes/{area}/{name}/…')`, copy the missing file into `public/resources/themes/{area}/{your-theme}/` (e.g. `preview.svg`). One file, one theme, no core edits.
3. **Admin UI settings** — theme Custom CSS/JS, options, branding uploads when the product already supports them.
4. **Extension hooks** from §3 — registries, rebinds, `routes/custom.php`, `bootstrap/providers.marketplace.php`.

### Avoid unless the user explicitly approves core changes

- Editing **`entrypoint.sh`**, **`composer.json`**, **`Dockerfile`**, **`package.json`**, or adding **`scripts/`** helpers to change how the whole app deploys or links assets.
- Replacing **`public/resources/themes/`** with a symlink/junction or bulk-syncing all themes — conflicts with the author’s shipped copy under `public/resources/themes/guest/localboostai/**` and is wiped or duplicated on update.
- Patching **`modules/**` helpers** (e.g. `theme_asset_for()`) for a single custom theme.
- “Fixing” by copying an entire theme tree into `public/` when only one static file is 404.

### Decision checklist

| Question | If yes → |
|----------|----------|
| Can this be fixed inside our custom theme folder only? | Do it there. |
| Is it a static URL 404 under `/resources/themes/...`? | Copy **only** that file to `public/resources/themes/{area}/{your-theme}/`. |
| Does the fix require changing author deploy/bootstrap/composer? | **Stop** — propose the minimal custom-zone alternative first. |
| Will author `git pull` / marketplace update overwrite this path? | Move the change out of §1 core paths into §2. |

### Example (theme preview 404)

- **Views** load from `resources/themes/guest/mlhubtheme/` (OK — custom theme source).
- **Preview thumbnail** is served from `public/resources/themes/guest/mlhubtheme/preview.svg` via `theme_asset_for()` (core behavior).
- **Correct fix:** keep `preview.svg` in the theme source **and** copy it to the matching `public/.../mlhubtheme/` path on deploy.
- **Wrong fix:** new link script, edit `entrypoint.sh`, or symlink all of `public/resources/themes`.

---

## 9. Forbidden without explicit user request

- Editing `composer.json`, `composer.lock`, `package.json`, `package-lock.json`, `Dockerfile`, `entrypoint.sh`.
- Editing `bootstrap/app.php` or `bootstrap/providers.php`.
- Editing core migrations, seeders, or any author route file.
- Editing `config/*.php` (use `.env` or merge custom config).
- Editing core themes or `resources/themes/shared/`.
- Running `migrate:fresh`, `migrate:rollback`, `db:wipe` on production.
- Force-push or rewriting author git history.
- Committing `.env`, API keys, or any file under `storage/` other than `.gitkeep`.

- Adding root-level **`scripts/`** or composer hooks to alter global asset linking (use custom-zone copies or user-approved deploy docs instead).

When unsure: **add** under `app/Custom/`, `modules/Custom*`, or your **custom theme name** (e.g. `mlhubtheme`) and register through `bootstrap/providers.marketplace.php`. Never patch core.
